  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the number of visitors last year.\n\nWe're told that attendance increased to $120%$ of last year’s total. Thus, the new number of visitors is $1.2x.$\n\nWe are also told that of those visitors, $90%$ attended the art exhibit. So, the number of visitors who attended the art exhibit is\n\n$$\n0.9(1.2x)=1.08x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $1.08x$ represents $108%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $108%$ of last year’s total attended the art exhibit.",
